COMMENT ON TABLE __mj."ScopedPromptConfig" IS 'A scope-aware override of an AIPrompt''s RUN SETTINGS (model/vendor, AI configuration, sampling knobs, response format, effort level). The run-settings sibling of ScopedPromptPart. Narrowed by a polymorphic scope (PrimaryScopeEntity/Record + SecondaryScopes). Resolved by a cached engine via a specificity cascade per PromptID — the most-specific in-scope row wins as a whole row (tie-broken by Priority); each non-null column overrides the prompt default, a NULL column inherits it. Runtime-explicit overrides on the agent run still win. Lets any MJ app tune model/generation behavior per scope by editing rows, not code.';

COMMENT ON COLUMN __mj."ScopedPromptConfig"."PromptID" IS 'The AIPrompt whose run settings this row overrides.';

COMMENT ON COLUMN __mj."ScopedPromptConfig"."Description" IS 'Optional human-readable note about this override (authoring aid; not sent to the model).';

COMMENT ON COLUMN __mj."ScopedPromptConfig"."PrimaryScopeRecordID" IS 'The record ID within the primary scope entity that this override is scoped to. NULL = global (applies regardless of scope). When set with empty SecondaryScopes, the override is primary-scope-only (e.g. org-level).';

COMMENT ON COLUMN __mj."ScopedPromptConfig"."SecondaryScopes" IS 'JSON object of additional scope dimensions (e.g. {"ChannelID":"..."}). Empty/NULL with PrimaryScopeRecordID set = primary-scope-only; populated = fully-scoped. Matched (cascading or strict) against the run''s SecondaryScopes.';

COMMENT ON COLUMN __mj."ScopedPromptConfig"."Status" IS 'Lifecycle: Active (live), Provisional (staged; eligible but flaggable as not-yet-final), Archived (excluded from resolution). Only Active and Provisional are eligible for resolution.';

COMMENT ON COLUMN __mj."ScopedPromptConfig"."Priority" IS 'Precedence / tie-break for resolution. Higher wins when two rows tie on scope specificity. Default 0.';

COMMENT ON COLUMN __mj."ScopedPromptConfig"."ModelID" IS 'Optional model override for this scope. NULL = use the prompt''s own model selection. Applied as AIPromptParams.override.modelId.';

COMMENT ON COLUMN __mj."ScopedPromptConfig"."VendorID" IS 'Optional vendor override paired with ModelID (which inference provider serves the model). NULL = let MJ pick. Applied as AIPromptParams.override.vendorId.';

COMMENT ON COLUMN __mj."ScopedPromptConfig"."ConfigurationID" IS 'Optional AI Configuration (environment) override for this scope. NULL = inherit. Applied as AIPromptParams.configurationId.';

COMMENT ON COLUMN __mj."ScopedPromptConfig"."Temperature" IS 'Sampling temperature override. NULL = inherit the prompt default. Applied via AIPromptParams.additionalParameters.';

COMMENT ON COLUMN __mj."ScopedPromptConfig"."TopP" IS 'Nucleus-sampling (top-p) override. NULL = inherit. Applied via additionalParameters.';

COMMENT ON COLUMN __mj."ScopedPromptConfig"."TopK" IS 'Top-k sampling override. NULL = inherit. Applied via additionalParameters.';

COMMENT ON COLUMN __mj."ScopedPromptConfig"."MinP" IS 'Min-p sampling override. NULL = inherit. Applied via additionalParameters.';

COMMENT ON COLUMN __mj."ScopedPromptConfig"."FrequencyPenalty" IS 'Frequency-penalty override. NULL = inherit. Applied via additionalParameters.';

COMMENT ON COLUMN __mj."ScopedPromptConfig"."PresencePenalty" IS 'Presence-penalty override. NULL = inherit. Applied via additionalParameters.';

COMMENT ON COLUMN __mj."ScopedPromptConfig"."Seed" IS 'Deterministic sampling seed override. NULL = inherit. Applied via additionalParameters.';

COMMENT ON COLUMN __mj."ScopedPromptConfig"."StopSequences" IS 'Comma-delimited stop sequences override. NULL = inherit. Applied via additionalParameters.';

COMMENT ON COLUMN __mj."ScopedPromptConfig"."ResponseFormat" IS 'Response-format override: Any, JSON, Markdown, ModelSpecific, or Text. NULL = inherit. Applied via additionalParameters.';

COMMENT ON COLUMN __mj."ScopedPromptConfig"."EffortLevel" IS 'Reasoning/effort level override (1-100). NULL = inherit the prompt default. Applied as AIPromptParams.effortLevel.';

